 "description": "Welded turret seen from above: Kontakt-5 block in front, then the cheek at ~59 deg to a frontal shot - 100 mm outer wall, ~250 mm cavity of 'reflecting' NERA modules (21 mm steel + 6 mm rubber + 3 mm steel, 22 mm gaps), 95 mm inner wall and a 45 mm high-hardness plate. Estimates vs long rods ~780-830 mm with Kontakt-5. Reconstruction from public sources (Tankograd, Below The Turret Ring, Zaloga/Wikipedia, forum analyses); real tank armour is secret. Armour amount = public protection estimate / mass efficiency (NERA ~1.3-1.5, Soviet arrays ~1.17). The explosive inside ERA is an empty gap until explosives are added, and the model under-represents NERA breaking long rods - so a full simulation is penetrated more easily than the real armour; the Tank check uses the estimates. 2D slice.",
